    "['ip [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family inet', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family inet', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family inet\\nset forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family mpls\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, a simpler equivalent in Junos would be:\\n##\\nset forwarding-options hash-key family inet\\n##\\n\\nNote: While `ip cef` (Cisco Express Forwarding) doesn't have a direct 1:1 equivalent in Junos, these commands configure similar optimized forwarding behavior. Junos uses a different forwarding architecture by default that provides similar benefits to CEF. The first option more closely matches CEF's behavior for both IPv4 and MPLS forwarding.\", 'trans_template': 'set forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family inet'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family mpls', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family mpls', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family inet\\nset forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family mpls\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, a simpler equivalent in Junos would be:\\n##\\nset forwarding-options hash-key family inet\\n##\\n\\nNote: While `ip cef` (Cisco Express Forwarding) doesn't have a direct 1:1 equivalent in Junos, these commands configure similar optimized forwarding behavior. Junos uses a different forwarding architecture by default that provides similar benefits to CEF. The first option more closely matches CEF's behavior for both IPv4 and MPLS forwarding.\", 'trans_template': 'set forwarding-options enhanced-hash-key family mpls'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options hash-key family inet', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set forwarding-options hash-key family inet', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset forwarding-options enh